.TH pepe 1  pepe "User Commands"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
pepe \- HTTP load generator
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpepe\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-number\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-concurrency\fR] [\fB\-z\fR|\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-curl\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-method\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-headers\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-body\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-user\-agent\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-proxy\fR] [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-insecure\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-compression\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-keepalive\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-redirects\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-snapshot\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-setup\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIURL\fR] [\fIARGS\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
HTTP load generator
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-number\fR \fI<NUMBER>\fR [default: 100]
Number of requests to perform
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-concurrency\fR \fI<CONCURRENCY>\fR [default: one per core]
Number of concurrent requests at a time
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Duration of the test, e.g. 10s, 3m, 2h (mutually exclusive with \-n)
.TP
\fB\-\-curl\fR
Load\-test a curl command: pepe \-\-curl \-\- curl \-X POST http://localhost:8080, or pass it as one quoted string, as @file, or on stdin
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-method\fR \fI<METHOD>\fR [default: GET]
HTTP method, e.g. GET, POST, PUT, DELETE
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-headers\fR \fI<HEADERS>\fR
HTTP headers, e.g. \-H \*(AqAccept: application/json\*(Aq
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR [default: 20]
Time in seconds to wait for a response
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Threads sending requests (default 1). One sends about 100k requests a second; the dashboard says when it is the limit
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-body\fR \fI<BODY>\fR
HTTP request body
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\-agent\fR \fI<USER_AGENT>\fR
User\-Agent string, default is pepe/{version}
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-proxy\fR \fI<PROXY>\fR
Proxy server URL: http://user:pass@host:port or socks5://host:port
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR
Accept invalid TLS certificates (self\-signed, expired, wrong host)
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-compression\fR
Disable HTTP compression, e.g. gzip
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-keepalive\fR
Disable HTTP keepalive, e.g. Connection: close
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-redirects\fR
Prevent http redirects
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output results in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshot\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write the JSON report so far to this file every minute while the run goes, and once more when it ends, so a long run\*(Aqs numbers survive a crash or a lost terminal; it has a minute\-by\-minute timeline of the whole run
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-setup\fR
Open the setup screen to review or change the settings before starting (it opens by itself when no URL is given)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIURL\fR] [default: ]
HTTP url to request
.TP
[\fIARGS\fR] [default: ]
List of arguments to pass to curl command
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pepe\-self\-update(1)
Update pepe to the latest release, or say what\*(Aqs new in it
.TP
pepe\-completions(1)
Tab completion for your shell: print the script, or \-\-install it
.TP
pepe\-api(1)
Load\-test every endpoint of an OpenAPI spec
.TP
pepe\-ramp(1)
Raise the load step by step to find where the target stops keeping up
.TP
pepe\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "DASHBOARD KEYS"
.TP
\fBspace, p\fR
Pause or resume sending; a timed run\*(Aqs clock stops while paused
.TP
\fB+, \-\fR
Raise or lower concurrency by about 10%, live
.TP
\fBs, i\fR
Stop sending and keep the results on screen
.TP
\fBr\fR
Restart with the same settings (and the current concurrency)
.TP
\fBE\fR
Back to the setup screen (or, in API mode, the plan)
.TP
\fBtab, left, right, 1\-3\fR
Switch view
.TP
\fBup, down, j, k, PgUp, PgDn, g, G\fR
Select a request in the log
.TP
\fBf\fR
Filter requests by status: 2xx, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx, no response, failed
.TP
\fBl\fR
Filter requests by latency: at or above p50, p90 or p99
.TP
\fB/\fR
Search the status and response text
.TP
\fBe, c\fR
Show only failed requests; clear all filters
.TP
\fBenter\fR
Inspect the selected request; esc goes back
.TP
\fB?\fR
Show all keys
.TP
\fBq, esc, Ctrl\-C\fR
Quit
.SH "SETUP SCREEN KEYS"
.TP
\fBtab\fR
Switch mode: Single URL, Ramp or API
.TP
\fBup, down\fR
Move between fields; left, right change a choice
.TP
\fBenter\fR
Start the run (or load the spec, in API mode)
.TP
\fBctrl\-t\fR
Send the request once and show the response
.TP
\fBesc\fR
Quit
.SH "RAMP KEYS"
.TP
\fBup, down\fR
Pick a step and see everything measured about it; esc follows the run again
.TP
\fBspace\fR
Pause or resume; a step\*(Aqs clock stops while paused
.TP
\fBn\fR
End this step now and go on to the next
.TP
\fBs\fR
Stop the ramp here and keep the results
.TP
\fBr, e\fR
Run again; back to the setup screen
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBpepe https://example.com\fR
100 requests, one per core at a time, with the dashboard
.TP
\fBpepe \-z 30s \-c 50 https://example.com\fR
Thirty seconds at concurrency 50
.TP
\fBpepe \-\-curl \-\- curl \-X POST https://httpbin.org/post \-d \*(Aq{"a":1}\*(Aq\fR
The request a curl command would send
.TP
\fBpepe ramp https://example.com \-\-to 200 \-\-until \*(Aqp99 > 500ms\*(Aq\fR
Raise the load until p99 passes 500 ms
.TP
\fBpepe \-\-json \-n 1000 https://example.com > results.json\fR
No dashboard; a JSON report
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBPEPE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK\fR
Set to anything to skip the look for a newer release
.TP
\fBPEPE_GITHUB_TOKEN\fR
A GitHub token for pepe self\-update, for forks or rate\-limited CI
.SH "SEE ALSO"
pepe\-ramp(1), pepe\-api(1), pepe\-self\-update(1), and \fBhttps://github.com/omarmhaimdat/pepe\fR
